; The cost of the matched posting is derived per unit onto the generated
; posting (src/xact.cc:1613-1624, "derive the cost from the annotation"),
; so the rule leaves a EUR residual on top of the imbalance that the top
; posting's cost already carried, and verify() rejects the transaction
; (src/xact.cc:1677-1684, verify at src/xact.cc:1040-1110).

= /Energy/
    Assets:Rebate    1

2026/01/01 power
    Expenses:Energy    100 kWh @@ 72.00 EUR
    Assets:Cash

test bal -> 1
__ERROR__
While parsing file "$FILE", line 12:
While balancing transaction from "$FILE", lines 10-12:
> 2026/01/01 power
>     Expenses:Energy    100 kWh @@ 72.00 EUR
>     Assets:Cash
Unbalanced remainder is:
               EUR72
Amount to balance against:
              EUR144
While applying automated transaction from "$FILE", lines 7-8:
> = /Energy/
>     Assets:Rebate    1
While extending transaction from "$FILE", lines 10-12:
> 2026/01/01 power
>     Expenses:Energy    100 kWh @@ 72.00 EUR
>     Assets:Cash
Error: Transaction does not balance
end test
